    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **57 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create-owner audit line is emitted by `AuditOwnerCreated.service(...)`. It already logged `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and `membershipLevel`. I added `membershipNumber`, deriving it exactly as the `OwnerMapper` does for the response DTO (`\"%s-M%02d\"` of the owner's `customerCode` and last-two-digits of the registration year), so the audit value matches what the API returns.\n\nChange to `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Compute `membershipNumber` from `owner.getCustomerCode()` and `owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100`.\n- Extend the log format/args with `membershipNumber={}`, keeping all previously logged fields intact.\n\nThe new `Cp43Tests` (which creates an owner, fetches it, and asserts the AUDIT log contains both the returned `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel`) passes, and all 57 tests remain green.",
